+# SA3DS 0.0.9.0G — White Zone Validation Gate
+
+This is a code-only Sonic Adventure 3DS development checkpoint. It contains no Sega game assets, owner-generated Sonic payloads, third-party mod payloads, `.3dsx`, or CIA.
+
+## Highlights
+
+- 10 contiguous deterministic White Zone sections including dedicated TURN.
+- 24-unit course width and 10-unit measurement markers retained.
+- Selected-zone fall/out-of-bounds fallback goes through the real physics reset path.
+- Bottom-screen parity HUD snapshot data for position, XYZ velocity, speed, heading, contact/slope, action, animation, trace and resource metrics.
+- FOLLOW and fixed REFERENCE measurement camera modes.
+- Extended per-frame White Zone CSV with test identity, movement/contact and animation fields.
+- Strict `REFERENCE.csv` vs `SA3DS.csv` comparator aligned by `(test_id, frame)`.
+- 12 deterministic protocols covering acceleration, coast, braking, low/high-speed turning, jump tap/hold, Spin Dash, Roll exit, slopes and air control.
+- 1,024-state proof that animation observation/selection remains presentation-only.
+
+## Evidence rule
+
+`VERIFIED 1:1` is only emitted for an exact trace match when the comparator is explicitly told that the reference is a live retail SADX capture. Otherwise exact/tolerance agreement is `MATCHES MEASURED FIELDS`. Global `PHYSICS_1TO1` remains false.
+
+## Build
+
+Use `build_0_0_9_0G.sh` after placing owner-generated `sonic.sa3c` and `sonic.sa3t` in `runtime_0_0_9_0G/romfs/sa3ds/`. devkitARM is required.
